29,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My heart sinks a little. The conservation lab is nearly empty, and our volunteers are mostly from one specific history circle.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Shion,,"As I suspected, paperwork delays from distant lenders have caused openings to slip. Powered displays are also a maintenance nightmare.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"This is interesting! People love it when someone is actually working or talking in the gallery, and mechanisms always draw a crowd.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The suspended bay has a strict weight limit, and our evening hires mean we can't have displays that can't be easily cleared or secured.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"I found it! Transport and insurance for loans are eating up a huge chunk of the budget, and joiner rates are going up!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, if powered displays are so troublesome, perhaps we should avoid them to spare our remaining staff.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, I agree. Complexity is the enemy of a timely opening. We need something that arrives on time and stays working.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"But @Shion, the data says ""boring"" doesn't work. We need movement or a human presence to keep the visitors coming back.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, movement is fine, but not if it exceeds the weight limit of the bay or gets knocked over by catering chairs during evening hires.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"And it has to be cheap! If we bring in too many fancy loans from far away, we'll run out of money again!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, you are quite right. We must be mindful of the costs and the people. A local focus might be kinder to everyone.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shion,,Local loans would certainly solve the paperwork and shipping cut-off issues I discovered. It reduces the variables of failure.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"Local is okay, but only if it's interactive. A room of static cases is a ghost town according to the head counts.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I am worried about the conservation backlog. Whatever we pick shouldn't require heavy cleaning or stabilization from a one-person lab.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Sakura,,Exactly! Let's pick something that doesn't need a million crates or expensive new mounts!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
