55,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at the candidates, Textiles of the Region seems lovely. It uses local craftspeople, which supports our volunteers and avoids the lab backlog.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Shion,,"City Under Excavation is tempting, but a working conservation bench might be too much for a lab that is already underwater.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,"Light and Motion would be a hit with the crowds, but @Shion mentioned powered displays are a disaster for maintenance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Maritime Trade Routes involves many loans, which @Sakura noted are expensive, and ship models might be bulky for the evening hire clearances.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Sakura,,I love the Textiles idea! Local things mean less money spent on scary shipping costs and fancy crates!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, the Textiles exhibition includes demonstration sessions. That provides the human presence the visitors crave without stressing the staff.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Shion,,"It also avoids the rigging and powered elements of Light and Motion, which would likely lead to the call-outs I saw in the logs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"I suppose demonstrations are a good substitute for kinetic art. It satisfies the ""human element"" the comment slips mentioned.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Misaki,,And textiles are lightweight. They won't threaten the structural limit of the suspended bay like the excavations' stonework might.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"It's a win-win! It's pretty, it's local, and it won't swallow the budget in transport fees!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel a great sense of peace with this choice. It honors the community and respects our current capacities.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Shion,,It is the most logical path. It minimizes the risk of shipping delays and maintenance failures.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,"I can sell this to the public. ""Living Traditions"" sounds much more exciting than a room of old charts.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Misaki,,It is the safest option for the building and the most sustainable for the staff. I am in agreement.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Yay! Let's do the Textiles one! It's the best mystery-solved choice!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am ready to vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Shion,,I concur. I vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,May,,I'm on board. I vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I also vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Me too! I vote for Textiles of the Region!,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
